    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0892" n="850" xml:id="pg850"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 398</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/8–251: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Spain
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d398-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-08-02T20:00:00-04:00">August 2, 1951—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. Joint State–ECA message.</p>
                <p>1. Fol are terms of reference of group ECA planning send Madrid about Aug 12 to
                    conduct special econ study Spain. Dr. Sidney C. Sufrin designated Chief,
                    Temporary Econ Survey Group. Sufrin responsible to and will report to ECA
                    Administrator.</p>
                <p>2. Amb, as senior rep for the US in Spain and as primary instrument of US policy
                    in Spain, will be responsible for giving guidance and gen direction to
                    activities Temporary Econ Survey Group to assure consistency of Group’s
                    activities with fon policy objectives of US and to assure a coordinated US
                    position in all relations with Span Govt. Chief, Temporary Econ Survey Group
                    shall keep Amb and other appropriate Emb officials as he designates fully and
                    currently informed matters arising within scope special study. Amb and other Emb
                    officials he designates shall keep Chief Group fully and currently informed on
                    matters relative to conduct of special study. Relationship between Emb and
                    Temporary Survey Group expected to be intimate and completely coop.</p>
                <p>3. Temp Econ Survey Group will be engaged fol functions: <list>
                        <label>(a)</label>
                        <item>Analyze present status of projects already committed on $62.5 million
                            Ex-Im loan under terms PL 759.</item>
                        <label>(b)</label>
                        <item>Appraise desirability and feasibility of committed and anticipated
                            projects.</item>
                        <label>(c)</label>
                        <item>Study Span econ to determine econ development requirements and
                            capabilities in event of possible further econ aid.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>4. Emb and Group will collaborate closely on study mentioned para 3(c) above.
                    Study shld be prepared on confidential basis view its relationship to and effect
                    on negots re mil facilities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
